{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792599731,"nonce":"1Nvpku2YMowxKPtviG649y1NTL8=","message":"Implemented diagnostics-based per-document analysis tracking, explicitly opted in by the built-in Rayzor registration (diagnosticProgress:true). Each document retains only an analysed version counter; open/edit starts activity, accepted current diagnostics (including empty and unversioned Rayzor results) finish it. Stale versioned diagnostics cannot finish a newer analysis. Close, crash/restart, stop and replay reset activity consistently. Rayzor currently emits unversioned diagnostics rather than work-done events, so this indicates awaiting document analysis, not percentage/workspace progress; versionless results have the protocol limitation that they cannot identify an older document version.\n\nThe existing Rayzor logo rotates while starting/restarting or analysing the active document. Tooltip and menu say indexing plus filename. Inactive document notifications do not invalidate the active status view. Activity updates bind the existing SVG attribute and text; the status/dropdown control keeps its identity. Ashui 4c03cb1a10de9c58a832bb0555bcb789fe341b4c allows reactive tooltip labels, adopted without duplicating dependency/native build caches.\n\nCore checks pass, including stale/current/empty/unversioned diagnostics, coalesced edits, inactive-file isolation, unchanged-sync notification counts, close/stop/restart, and non-opt-in servers. The existing bin/rayzor executable also passes: opened document is analysing, its diagnostics clear activity, and 32 concurrent semantic hover requests preserve the session. Dark/light LSP snapshots assert animation active while indexing, fully stopped when ready, live update of an open tooltip and unchanged status-control identity. Reviewed bin/lsp-indexing-snapshots/rayde-{dark,light}-lsp-server-indexing.png. Logs: bin/lsp-indexing-checks.log, bin/lsp-indexing-real-checks.log, bin/lsp-indexing-snapshots.log. Native executable and macOS bundle rebuilding.","files":null}]}